1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,320
Please? We won't make it
in time for the festival.

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:06,850
I still can't allow you
to stay on campus overnight.

3
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:08,520
Do we pull an all-nighter
at somebody's place?

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,430
If none of your places work...

5
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:13,260
Pretty spacious, Mayama.

6
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:16,380
I'm ready to work all night.

7
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:18,320
I'm sorry we imposed.

8
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:21,010
We all invited ourselves over, day of.

9
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:22,230
It's fine.

10
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:26,830
I want our haunted house to be a success.

11
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:31,140
In middle school,
my friends often made fun of me.

12
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:33,190
Dude, obviously we were joking.

13
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:35,560
She'd never confess to a guy like you.

14
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:37,450
- Exactly!
- <i>To them,</i>

15
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:41,020
<i>it was all a joke.</i>

16
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:44,540
Asamiya. I'm happy you told me how you felt.

17
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,960
And I want to believe you, I really do.

18
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:50,460
But I can't help it. I'm still scared.

19
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:58,710
So, could you wait?

20
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:02,650
I'll wait as long as you need me to.

21
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,710
And don't feel forced to answer, either.

22
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:14,570
When you have a break during the festival,

23
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:19,370
do you want to check out
the other set-ups together?

24
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:24,790
Yeah. I want to eat crepes.

25
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:27,720
Sounds good.

26
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:30,750
Mayama?

27
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:54,430
[Tenn Mayama (Esteemed brother)]

28
00:01:56,610 --> 00:01:58,530
Hello?

29
00:01:58,530 --> 00:01:59,800
<i>Asamiya?</i>

30
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:00,990
Good morning.

31
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:05,230
<i>I'm sorry, Hare can't make it
to the festival today.</i>

32
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,720
Huh?

33
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:14,940
[Kitahara High Culture Festival]

34
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:18,000
- Looks good.
- Let me grab a pic.

35
00:02:21,670 --> 00:02:23,320
[Haunted House]

36
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,610
Grab our supplies.
[Haunted House]

37
00:02:25,610 --> 00:02:27,710
Thanks.
[Haunted House]

38
00:02:31,130 --> 00:02:34,450
Yikes. Keep it up!

39
00:02:34,450 --> 00:02:36,780
Where's Mayama?

40
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:39,430
Did you hear anything from him?

41
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:40,780
No.

42
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,100
Maybe he overslept?

43
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:45,750
- He's not you, you know.
- Hey!

44
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:50,150
Tell Haru I told him to rest up.

45
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:52,510
<i>We'll handle things just fine.</i>

46
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:54,420
Sorry, I know it's sudden.

47
00:02:55,490 --> 00:02:56,910
No worries at all.

48
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:58,990
<i>Wait.</i>

49
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:01,120
<i>Asamiya...</i>

50
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:06,480
<i>Please don't tell anyone I'm sick.</i>

51
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,880
Huh?

52
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:10,490
<i>I'll do something about it.</i>

53
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:12,290
What do you mean?

54
00:03:40,790 --> 00:03:44,310
We've got a line forming.

55
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:47,260
Guess we'll have to start without Mayama.

56
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,840
Are we using this Dracula costume?

57
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:56,180
Nah. Put it in storage for now.

58
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:58,260
- Sure.
- Wait.

59
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:01,650
If...

60
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:05,920
If Mayama doesn't show...

61
00:04:06,670 --> 00:04:08,510
I'll...

62
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:14,710
Sorry I'm late.

63
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,870
Asamiya, you handle the rest, okay?

64
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:09,510
- Sure.
- All right.

65
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:13,530
Who was that guy anyway?

66
00:05:13,530 --> 00:05:15,770
Beats me.

67
00:05:15,770 --> 00:05:18,420
One of our helpers?

68
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:21,070
Did you go see a doctor?

69
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,710
Yeah.

70
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:26,020
I also took some medicine, so I'm fine now.

71
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,450
Huh?

72
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,480
You're still a bit warm.

73
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,140
Don't push yourself, okay?

74
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,780
But...

75
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,340
It's not your fault you're sick.

76
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:48,850
I'll tell the others what's going on.

77
00:05:54,610 --> 00:05:56,910
I want to push through.

78
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:05,360
We all worked so hard on this.

79
00:06:06,290 --> 00:06:08,270
<i>Try them on.</i>

80
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:10,160
<i>Scare you?</i>

81
00:06:16,130 --> 00:06:18,760
If I push through till the end,

82
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:25,410
I think I'll come to like myself a bit more.

83
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:30,330
So, please.

84
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:38,980
Make a face like that,

85
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:42,340
and you know I can't stop you.

86
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:54,370
Fine. But I have one condition.

87
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:56,210
What is it?

88
00:06:57,550 --> 00:07:01,010
Leave enough strength
to go around the festival with me.

89
00:07:05,270 --> 00:07:06,800
Of course.

90
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:10,630
I promised, didn't I?

91
00:07:25,410 --> 00:07:27,750
[Haunted House]
[CAUTION]

92
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,750
Looking good, Mayama.

93
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:36,050
You're paving new frontiers for werewolves.

94
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:38,290
Am I supposed to be happy about that?

95
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:40,060
Can I snag a pic?

96
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:41,490
Sure.

97
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:49,400
All right. Let's do this.

98
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,420
- Right.
- Come in.

99
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,060
You too, Mayama.

100
00:07:56,590 --> 00:07:58,650
Repeat after me.

101
00:07:58,650 --> 00:08:02,320
Ready? Victory!

102
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,800
- Victory?
- Victory...

103
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,670
I guess?

104
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:08,070
Don't sound so skeptical.

105
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,280
Why, "victory"?

106
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,220
It was the first word I thought of.

107
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:12,640
Pick a better word next time.

108
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,330
Hey, rude!

109
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:18,450
- Quit pestering me about it!
- I'm just saying.

110
00:08:18,450 --> 00:08:20,070
Hello there!

111
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:21,280
Thanks for coming!

112
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:24,840
Please take a pamphlet.

113
00:08:30,290 --> 00:08:33,230
No way, no way.

114
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:34,910
There's definitely something here.

115
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:37,670
I can sense it.

116
00:08:39,010 --> 00:08:41,900
I'm scared already!

117
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,990
Oh my gosh.

118
00:08:45,990 --> 00:08:49,330
- Do you see something?
- I think so.

119
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:52,240
- Did that doll move?
- Maybe?

120
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:58,090
Roar!

121
00:08:59,110 --> 00:09:02,010
Louder.

122
00:09:02,010 --> 00:09:03,280
Yes, ma'am.

123
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:05,130
I think he's loud enough.

124
00:09:05,130 --> 00:09:06,910
Definitely not.

125
00:09:06,910 --> 00:09:10,100
Trust me, I'm a former theater kid.

126
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:13,910
Just a minute, we're almost ready!

127
00:09:13,910 --> 00:09:15,670
Now, repeat after me.

128
00:09:15,670 --> 00:09:18,080
Roar!

129
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,800
- Roar.
- Roar!

130
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:22,760
- Roar!
- Roar!

131
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,310
- Roar!
- Roar!

132
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:28,690
- Roar!
- Roar!

133
00:09:28,690 --> 00:09:30,720
[Entrance]

134
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,520
Roar!

135
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:36,700
Roar!

136
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,800
Great work, team!
[Haunted House on break until 1 P.M.]

137
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:50,620
Great work.

138
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:52,620
Our haunted house is a hit on social media.

139
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:54,990
People are especially praising our werewolf.

140
00:09:54,990 --> 00:09:57,190
Yeah, you're doing great, Mayama!

141
00:09:57,190 --> 00:09:59,770
You upped your game by the end there.

142
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:01,570
Thanks.

143
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,470
- Mayama?
- I'm fine.

144
00:10:05,470 --> 00:10:08,060
Just got a bit dizzy.

145
00:10:11,910 --> 00:10:13,620
Since when?

146
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:18,490
You're going to the infirmary.

147
00:10:18,490 --> 00:10:20,930
I'm fine. I just need to take more medicine.

148
00:10:20,930 --> 00:10:23,220
You need to treat yourself better.

149
00:10:25,050 --> 00:10:27,290
Is he feeling sick?

150
00:10:27,290 --> 00:10:29,990
Yeah. Cover for me until I'm back.

151
00:10:35,190 --> 00:10:37,290
No...

152
00:10:37,290 --> 00:10:39,560
I have to get back.

153
00:10:41,210 --> 00:10:44,130
Leave the rest to us, Mayama.

154
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:07,510
You awake?

155
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,500
The haunted house...

156
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,390
The festival's over.

157
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:20,970
Asamiya told us you were sick.

158
00:11:20,970 --> 00:11:23,270
Sorry we didn't notice.

159
00:11:23,270 --> 00:11:25,590
We must've been pushing you.

160
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,510
Oh...

161
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:34,550
It's over.

162
00:11:35,950 --> 00:11:38,350
I see.

163
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,550
Even though...

164
00:11:44,830 --> 00:11:46,130
<i>Not the time.</i>

165
00:11:46,130 --> 00:11:48,110
<i>Aw, no practice?</i>

166
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:04,540
We all worked so hard...

167
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:08,520
I ruined it.

168
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:12,010
It's my fault.

169
00:12:14,470 --> 00:12:16,170
I'm so sorry.

170
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:22,670
Nothing was "ruined".

171
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:25,930
- Huh?
- If anything, we had a roaring success.

172
00:12:25,930 --> 00:12:28,630
Thanks to a last minute, first-rate helper.

173
00:12:28,630 --> 00:12:30,610
Helper?

174
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:37,740
Asamiya...

175
00:12:37,740 --> 00:12:39,740
You're awake.

176
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:41,110
Glad to see you're okay.

177
00:12:41,110 --> 00:12:44,760
Did you step in for me?

178
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:48,090
Dracula-Asamiya brought in
a crazy amount of customers.

179
00:12:48,090 --> 00:12:49,560
What?

180
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:57,790
- Wait, he's super hot.
- Oh my god!

181
00:12:57,790 --> 00:12:59,560
He totally is!

182
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:01,530
He's so good-looking!

183
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:06,490
We wanted Asamiya to inherit
your role as werewolf.

184
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:11,200
But he insisted the werewolf
was your role alone.

185
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:15,500
Of course. I could never surpass
such perfect casting.

186
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:20,260
Should we leave you to it?

187
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:21,730
- Yeah.
- We're heading out already?

188
00:13:21,730 --> 00:13:23,630
Duh. We have to finish cleaning up.

189
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:25,090
Come on.

190
00:13:38,190 --> 00:13:42,840
Thanks for covering for me.

191
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:50,370
Just worry about yourself for now.

192
00:13:57,220 --> 00:13:58,850
Mayama?

193
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:04,710
I really am useless after all.

194
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,890
I'm sure you didn't enjoy

195
00:14:11,890 --> 00:14:14,940
getting dressed up for people, either.

196
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:21,830
This was the least I could do for you.

197
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:29,000
Besides, now I know what it's like
to act for someone else.

198
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,880
It's like I was in your shoes for once.

199
00:14:38,310 --> 00:14:44,110
Were you okay with me taking your place?

200
00:14:49,170 --> 00:14:51,380
You should lie down.

201
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:58,030
Sorry.

202
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:03,790
Let me stay like this.

203
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,270
The Dracula in me...

204
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:17,330
May lose his control.

205
00:15:17,330 --> 00:15:21,120
Dracula only acts at night.

206
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:27,900
That sort of logic doesn't apply
to Amamiya-Dracula.

207
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:33,460
I know you don't mean it.

208
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:43,880
You're always considerate of my feelings.

209
00:15:46,410 --> 00:15:53,040
I'm always your priority.

210
00:15:55,950 --> 00:16:01,340
While you were at the doctor's this morning,

211
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:04,140
I received a call from your older brother.

212
00:16:06,950 --> 00:16:10,430
<i>I'm sorry for all the trouble.</i>

213
00:16:10,430 --> 00:16:14,770
It's fine. I'm more worried about Haru.

214
00:16:14,770 --> 00:16:19,310
<i>I think Haru will go,
no matter what the doctor says.</i>

215
00:16:20,340 --> 00:16:23,990
Did you hear about his time in middle school?

216
00:16:23,990 --> 00:16:26,820
<i>A bit.</i>

217
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:29,920
Our parents are often out the house for work,

218
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:33,310
and Haru never feels like he can talk to me.

219
00:16:33,310 --> 00:16:37,060
<i>So, I'm really grateful to you, Asamiya.</i>

220
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,530
I haven't done anything though.

221
00:16:39,530 --> 00:16:43,550
<i>Haru really seems to be
enjoying himself these days.</i>

222
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:46,680
Which is exactly why

223
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:50,140
he's afraid he'll end up alone again.

224
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:53,350
I can tell he's desperate

225
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:57,970
to live up to everyone's expectations.

226
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:06,240
Don't force yourself
to live up to expectations.

227
00:17:07,350 --> 00:17:11,480
Don't put yourself down, either.

228
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,930
<i>Since that day we changed seats,</i>

229
00:17:14,930 --> 00:17:18,820
<i>and I decided to confess to you,</i>

230
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:23,390
I've gotten to know you much better.

231
00:17:23,390 --> 00:17:28,160
I also know what you consider your faults.

232
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:34,810
But all that has made me
fall for you even more.

233
00:17:39,870 --> 00:17:42,290
So...

234
00:17:42,290 --> 00:17:46,400
Please don't ever think lowly of yourself.

235
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:21,350
Mayama?

236
00:18:24,590 --> 00:18:27,150
Are you still asleep?

237
00:18:27,150 --> 00:18:30,120
We have to close up school soon.

238
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:31,960
I'll be coming in, okay?

239
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,080
Were you awake?

240
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,070
Yes.

241
00:18:38,070 --> 00:18:41,970
How do you feel?
Can you get home by yourself?

242
00:18:41,970 --> 00:18:43,870
Ms. Komori.

243
00:18:43,870 --> 00:18:46,270
Your face...

244
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:53,840
I helped fill in your shoes, too.

245
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:57,130
Scaring guests was just so much fun!

246
00:18:58,370 --> 00:18:59,590
I see.

247
00:18:59,590 --> 00:19:03,360
Now get yourself home, all right?

248
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:05,060
Yes, ma'am.

249
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:23,280
You okay?

250
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:26,050
Yeah, I'll manage.

251
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,870
What?

252
00:19:32,870 --> 00:19:36,610
I forgot to take a video of your werewolf.

253
00:19:36,610 --> 00:19:38,420
I only took a picture.

254
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:40,660
A picture's worth a thousand words, right?

255
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,300
Let's go.

256
00:19:57,650 --> 00:20:00,610
<i>I want to touch him.</i>

257
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:07,810
<i>I want to monopolize that expression of his.</i>

258
00:20:09,610 --> 00:20:13,830
Let's go around
the festival together next year.

259
00:20:13,830 --> 00:20:16,730
Yeah. You'd better.

260
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,800
I guess I'll take the video next year.

261
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:23,300
A haunted house, two years in a row?

262
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:25,110
Really?

263
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:33,950
<i>I think I'm ready.</i>

264
00:20:33,950 --> 00:20:39,050
<i>I'm finally ready
to give Asamiya my answer.</i>

265
00:20:39,910 --> 00:20:42,310
See you tomorrow.

266
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:47,130
And one more thing, Mayama.

267
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:55,180
You don't have to come to like me, okay?

268
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:00,870
Huh?

269
00:21:00,870 --> 00:21:05,030
I was satisfied enough confessing to you.

270
00:21:05,030 --> 00:21:07,200
I won't ask for anything more.

271
00:21:08,510 --> 00:21:10,390
- But...
- Besides,

272
00:21:10,390 --> 00:21:14,140
you're lovable to me

273
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:17,570
like a local mascot would be.

274
00:21:17,570 --> 00:21:21,000
Nothing more than that.

275
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:27,830
What the heck?

276
00:21:32,590 --> 00:21:36,410
I was serious.

277
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:38,950
Mayama?

278
00:21:39,870 --> 00:21:41,820
Whatever.

279
00:21:53,070 --> 00:21:54,220
Welcome home.

280
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:56,700
How are you feeling?

281
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,910
Haru?

282
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:08,100
What do you mean, a mascot?

283
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:23,340
<i>It was all a big misunderstanding?</i>

284
00:22:35,710 --> 00:22:39,830
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

285
00:22:44,670 --> 00:22:48,120
Now I've fallen for you for real.

286
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:12,990
I should've known.

287
00:24:12,990 --> 00:24:17,610
Of course Asamiya wasn't serious about me.

288
00:24:17,610 --> 00:24:19,650
You gotta give it one more push, Mayama.

289
00:24:19,650 --> 00:24:21,380
Who's ready to sing?

290
00:24:21,380 --> 00:24:23,450
- What's going on?
- Isn't that obvious?

291
00:24:23,450 --> 00:24:25,070
This is a mixer.

292
00:24:25,070 --> 00:24:28,810
I wanted to stay by your side

293
00:24:28,810 --> 00:24:30,670
all summer, Mayama.

294
00:24:30,670 --> 00:24:31,950
You're being unfair.

295
00:24:31,950 --> 00:24:34,190
If your feelings are a mess, tell him.

296
00:24:34,190 --> 00:24:36,950
He'll understand.

297
00:24:36,950 --> 00:24:40,740
What I want isn't so simple, though.

298
00:24:40,740 --> 00:24:42,070
Go home.

299
00:24:42,070 --> 00:24:45,300
You're the one
who drew the line first, Asamiya.

300
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:48,140
You're going through a tough romance, buddy.

301
00:24:48,140 --> 00:24:50,330
Tell me the truth.

302
00:24:50,330 --> 00:24:54,290
Did you do this sort of thing with Sakaki?

